{
	title: 'read_url tool: a web page as readable text',
	spec: 'A `read_url` model tool (src/host/tools/read_url.ts, tool name read_url) fetches one http(s) URL and returns readable text. Other schemes are an error result and fetch nothing. HTML becomes simple text: scripts, styles and markup dropped, block elements as line breaks, entities decoded, runs of blank lines collapsed; the page title first. Plain text and JSON pass through. When extracting text finds no readable content (including a JavaScript-only HTML shell or empty text response), the result explicitly says the page was empty or may require JavaScript and gives its URL; it never silently returns an empty success, and does not render JavaScript or use an external proxy. An image (png, jpeg, gif, webp) comes back as an image part the model sees, within the attachment size cap. Any other content type is saved under paths.fileDir (/tmp/hal/file/) and the result gives its path, type and size so bash can open it. Output is capped like read (50k chars) with a note of how much was cut. The body is never held whole beyond a bound: text and HTML read at most 10 MB (saying the page was longer), an image at most the attachment cap, and a download streams to its file. Redirects are followed; a non-2xx status is an error result with the status; a 30 s timeout and the turn abort signal cancel. Stdlib only: no HTML parser dependency. Artifact old-read-url.ts (reference). Tests with a local Bun.serve: HTML to text, an empty JavaScript app shell and empty plain text, the scheme check, the cap, an image part, a binary saved to a file, an endless text body cut at its limit.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Tool results keep fetched images as session blob references (image field), not embedded base64 in history; provider adapters replay image data from the blob. paths.fileDir() with no name is the download directory; with a name remains the pasted-file path. HTML is handled with a small regex/entity pass. Startup timing test can fail under parallel builds; other tests, tsc and lint passed.',
		'A read_url result must fit within tools.maxChars including its truncation note, so tools.run cannot truncate that note again and report the wrong amount cut.'
	],
	needs: [
		'sj'
	]
}
